    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Solve $|x|-2<4-x^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2<x<2$.",
      "worked": "$$|x|<6-x^2$$\nFor $x\\ge0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&<6-x^2\\\\x^2+x-6&<0\\\\(x+3)(x-2)&<0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $-3<x<2$. Restricting to $x\\ge0$ gives $0\\le x<2$.\n\nFor $x<0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}-x&<6-x^2\\\\x^2-x-6&<0\\\\(x-3)(x+2)&<0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $-2<x<3$. Restricting to $x<0$ gives $-2<x<0$.\n\nCombining the two cases gives $-2<x<2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 71
  },
